preConditionHook:
// NO PAUSE SINCE THE SESSION OPENED: each of the last noPauseBars bars made a
// higher high than the bar before it (mirror: a lower low), and enough bars
// have printed this session that the whole run lies INSIDE the session.
//
// Brooks reads the run as raising the odds of a reversal by the third or
// fourth bar, so the natural placement is NEGATED as a with-trend filter, or
// as written as a countertrend permission. Only the odds statement is
// discretionary; the bar test is not.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: a session starts when the
// wall-clock close date changes -- day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)),
// the EasyLanguage twin's date > date[1]. barsIn is 1 on the session's FIRST
// bar, SessionOpeningRange's convention. THE GUARD IS barsIn >= noPauseBars,
// exactly as the merged pseudocode writes it: that is what keeps the run's
// oldest compared bar, high[noPauseBars], from reaching into the previous
// session, and it is NOT a restriction to the session's first bars -- the rule
// can fire on any later bar whose run is wholly inside the session.
//
// The all-of-N loops start from the barsIn guard and let any failing bar clear
// the flag -- StrongTrendBarRun's arrangement -- so the loops run
// unconditionally and EasyLanguage's lack of short-circuiting cannot matter.
// The flags are class members and persist across bars, so both are set at the
// top rather than relied on to start true.
//
// The date comparison is on integer day serials, not prices, so it is exact
// and does not go through el_gt; the bar-count comparison is cast to double
// for the EL relational because noPauseBars is an input.
//
// WARM-UP: barsIn starts at 0 like every EL variable, so a first calculated
// bar falling mid-session under-counts until the first date change. That is
// EL's behaviour, mirrored rather than corrected. Intraday bars only.
//
// Deepest bar touched: noPauseBars.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    barsIn = 1;
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
}
noPauseUp = el_ge((double)barsIn, noPauseBars);
noPauseDn = el_ge((double)barsIn, noPauseBars);
for (int k = 0; k < (int)noPauseBars; ++k) {
    if (el_le(high[k], high[k + 1])) noPauseUp = false;
    if (el_ge(low[k], low[k + 1])) noPauseDn = false;
}
